{{! The image's own partials/standard_headers.hbs, changed in what a page is
    drawn in and what its tab says. The image's layouts include it in the head
    of every page but the welcome layout, which `welcome.hbs` replaces: the
    login, consent, logout and error pages among them.

    THE FAVICON IS CHUGGY'S, `favicon.svg`, which is served beside this sheet
    from the image's `public/`. The image's names `favico.png`, Ory's mark,
    through a value every route is handed; this does not read it.

    THE TITLE NAMES CHUGGY, after the name the image's route gives its page:
    `Sign in · chuggy`, `Consent · chuggy`, `Logout · chuggy`.

    `chuggy.css` IS LINKED LAST, because it sets the properties the image's
    `theme.css` sets, on the same element, and the later wins.

    THE IMAGE'S FONTS ARE NOT LOADED. Its Inter and JetBrains Mono are
    preloaded and declared here in the image's partial, and `chuggy.css` names
    the console's faces, which are the reader's own system's; the three
    Font Awesome sheets stay, because a card draws the GitHub button's mark
    from them.

    READ AGAINST THE IMAGE
    sha256:46a7bac1ad0c67c692b37d0380613fd4618fd751afac2c5314aa8d3ae77ef1f0
    because every sheet above but the last is that image's, at the path it
    serves it from, and the image's layouts are what include this partial. An
    image that served another sheet a card needs would have it drawn unstyled
    here. So tests/ory-ui-view.py holds ory-ui.yaml to that image and to the
    path it reads this partial from, and another is named here once its pages
    have been looked at under this one. }}
